==============================================================================
DIVIDER (2Div) -- SWEEP AND REPORT
==============================================================================

Scripts for PVT simulation of the 2Div frequency divider in ngspice and for
verifying that the signal is correctly divided on the div2 ... div128 branches.


FILES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
run_sweep.sh        Sweep driver: corner x temperature x VDD. Patches the
                    testbench, runs `ngspice -b`, and finally calls the report
                    script.

plot_divider.py     Loads the .dat files, computes frequency and duty cycle of
                    each branch, checks divisibility, and generates an HTML
                    report (tables only, no plots).


DIRECTORY LAYOUT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The scripts assume the same project structure as the other blocks:

  PROJECT_DIR/
  |-- configs/
  |   `-- corner_data          # t_min/t_nom/t_max, vp_min/vp_nom/vp_max, corners
  |-- divider/
  |   |-- scripts/
  |   |   |-- run_sweep.sh       # <- this file
  |   |   `-- plot_divider.py    # <- this file
  |   |-- simulations/
  |   |   `-- 2Div_tb.spice      # testbench
  |   `-- results/
  |       |-- data/              # generated *.dat
  |       `-- divider_report.html  # generated report

run_sweep.sh derives PROJECT_DIR as the directory two levels above the script
itself, so run it from divider/scripts/.


REQUIREMENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- ngspice on PATH
- python3 with numpy
- a configs/corner_data file providing: t_min t_nom t_max,
  vp_min vp_nom vp_max, corners (a list, e.g. "mos_tt mos_ss mos_ff ...")


RUNNING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  cd divider/scripts

  ./run_sweep.sh                 # full sweep: all corners x all PVT points
  ./run_sweep.sh -c typ          # mos_tt, t_nom, vp_nom
  ./run_sweep.sh -c hot          # mos_ss, t_max, vp_min
  ./run_sweep.sh -c cold         # mos_ff, t_min, vp_max
  ./run_sweep.sh -c hot cold     # several presets at once
  ./run_sweep.sh -c tt ss        # corners by name (substring match)

Presets narrow corner + temperature + VDD. Passing only a corner name (e.g.
"tt") narrows the corner only; temperature and VDD use their full ranges.


WHAT IS MEASURED
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For each PVT combination the script records the waveforms:

  wrdata <dat> v(clk) v(div2) v(div4) v(div8) v(div16) v(div32) v(div64) v(div128)

Over the last 50% of the simulation (the flip-flop chain must settle first),
plot_divider.py computes:

  - clk           : frequency and duty cycle (reference clock)
  - div2..div128  : frequency, duty cycle, and the measured divider ratio
                    f_clk / f_divN (which should equal N)

Frequency and duty are averaged over all periods in the analysis window
(interpolated crossings of the 50% amplitude level).


PASS/FAIL CRITERION (green check / red X)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A branch gets a green check when it meets BOTH conditions:

  1. the measured divider ratio matches the expected N (10% relative tolerance)
  2. the duty cycle is within 50% +/- 5%

Otherwise it gets a red X. A branch that does not toggle (stuck node) reports a
measured divider of N/A and also fails.


REPORT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/divider_report.html contains:

  - Summary: a per-corner table with f_clk, clk duty, the number of correct
    branches (e.g. 7/7), and an overall status.

  - One panel per PVT combination: a table with a clk row (reference) and rows
    for div2..div128 showing measured/expected frequency, expected/measured
    divider ratio, duty cycle, and status.

Duty cells are highlighted (orange for deviation > 5%, red for > 10%), and a
mismatched measured divider is highlighted in red.


TUNABLE PARAMETERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In plot_divider.py (constants near the top):

  - DUTY_TARGET, DUTY_TOL : duty-cycle center and tolerance (default 50% +/-5%)
  - DIV_REL_TOL           : divider-match tolerance (default 0.10)
  - LAST_FRACTION         : fraction of the simulation fed to analysis (def 0.5)
  - the 0.40 * vdd threshold in analyze_signal : minimum swing counted as real
    switching (rejects stuck nodes)

In run_sweep.sh:

  - tran 50p 4u : time step and stop time. At ~320 MHz clock this gives ~10
    periods of the slowest branch (div128); increase it if the chain starts
    up slowly.
  - the block that rewrites the ".lib cornerMOSlv.lib <corner>" line : the
    corner sweep only works if the names in corner_data (mos_tt, mos_ss, ...)
    match the library. If your flow selects the corner differently, remove
    that re.sub.

NOTE: the order of signals in the wrdata line (run_sweep.sh) must match
SIGNAL_ORDER in plot_divider.py. If you change one, change the other.
